WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.630
 I think we look at it as such a larger

00:00:02.630 --> 00:00:03.160
 scale.

00:00:03.160 --> 00:00:04.840
 I'm really big, especially when I deal

00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:05.520
 with individuals

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:07.820
 celebrating these small wins.

00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:10.840
 So it's about a person just showing up

00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:14.010
 and allowing me to even expound on

00:00:14.010 --> 00:00:14.280
 something

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:16.400
 is a win for me, right?

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:19.600
 Them say, "Hey, Cornelius, hey, yes,

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:21.640
 I'm gonna make your appointment at nine o'clock

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:23.760
 and be showing up, especially because I

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:24.720
 work a lot

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:27.120
 out of men's shelters and women's

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:27.600
 shelters,

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:30.400
 and really a transient population."

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:33.800
 For them just to show up and just listen

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.160
 for 15 minutes,

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:38.320
 20 minutes, it's the win.

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:41.480
 As you build on that, it's like grains of

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:42.760
 sand on a beach.

00:00:42.760 --> 00:00:45.320
 Just keep dropping them grains of sand.

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:47.220
 Next thing you know, you got a beautiful

00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:47.720
 beach.

00:00:47.720 --> 00:00:49.520
 It's about creating the opportunity

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:52.040
 to drop the grain of sand, in my opinion.

00:00:52.040 --> 00:00:53.400
 So that's the biggest wins.

